<title>GREECE: NATL MORTGAGE BANK CUTS MORTGAGE, DEPO RATES.</title>
<headline>NATL MORTGAGE BANK CUTS MORTGAGE, DEPO RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Mortgage Bank of Greece</p>
<p>will cut its mortgage, consumer loan and savings</p>
<p>deposit rates by 25 to 75 basis points, effective April 14, it</p>
<p>said on Friday.</p>
<p>It will offer the following rate structure:</p>
<p>CONSUMER LENDING</p>
<p>    ** Consumer loan		   24.5 from 25  percent</p>
<p>    ** Credit Card		     24.5 from 25</p>
<p>MORTGAGES</p>
<p>    ** Three-year			12.5 from 13.25 percent</p>
<p>    ** Six-year			  13.0 from 13.75</p>
<p>    ** 10-, 15-year fixed	    13.75 from 14.25</p>
<p>    ** 10-,15-, 20-year floating   15.75 from 16.0</p>
<p>DEPOSITS</p>
<p>    ** Savings deposit		 9.25  percent</p>
<p>    ** Housing savings		 9.25</p>
<p>    ** Preferred savings	     9.75</p>
<p>	 10-20 million drs	    10.25</p>
<p>	 20-50 million drs	    10.50</p>
<p>	 over 50 million drs	  10.75</p>
<p>** Time deposits</p>
<p>	 Three-months		    9.5   percent</p>
<p>	 Six months			9.75</p>
<p>	 12 months			10.0</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
